    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Evening fevers to 38.6 °C with night sweats for about four weeks</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R50.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting symptom, superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Weight loss of 5 kg over two months (57 to 52 kg), with poor appetite</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R63.4</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting symptom, superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Dull right upper quadrant pain for three weeks, worse on deep breathing and lying on the right side, with a tender liver edge</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R10.11</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting symptom, superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Amebic liver abscess: a single 6.2 x 5.4 cm abscess in the right lobe (segment VII) on ultrasound, Entamoeba histolytica antibody positive, blood cultures negative, years after two episodes of dysentery in India; treated with metronidazole and then paromomycin; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the hepatic amoebiasis later proposed for his illness</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>A06.4</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis; it does not settle the historical diagnostic conflict (CLM-0010, CLM-0011).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Vitamin B12 deficiency from a strict vegetarian diet (B12 168 pg/mL), with anemia (hemoglobin 11.2 g/dL, MCV 99 fL) to which inflammation also contributes</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D51.3</td><td>S — Synthetic finding anchored to his documented diet and the vitamin deficiency later proposed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Vitamin D deficiency (25-hydroxyvitamin D 9 ng/mL)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>E55.9</td><td>S — Synthetic finding anchored to his documented diet and the vitamin deficiency later proposed.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-7">
    <td>Positive interferon-gamma release assay, with chest radiograph and sputum smears and NAAT negative for tuberculosis; cultures pending</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R76.12</td><td>S — Synthetic finding, superseded by the diagnosis of latent infection when cultures were negative.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-9">
    <td>Adjustment disorder with depressed mood (PHQ-9 12, no thoughts of self-harm) during a serious illness, far from his wife and family</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>F43.21</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis anchored to his documented loneliness; not a claim about his real mental health.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

